<section class="race-expectations-leaders" aria-label="Top 3 and Flop 3 versus expectation">
  <div class="race-expectations-leader-grid">
    <% [["Top 3", "Beat the estimate", report.top_three, "positive"], ["Flop 3", "Below the estimate", report.flop_three, "negative"]].each do |title, subtitle, entries, tone| %>
      <article class="race-expectations-leaderboard race-analysis-<%= tone %>" aria-label="<%= title %>">
        <header><h4><%= title %></h4><span><%= subtitle %></span></header>
        <% if entries.any? %>
          <ol>
            <% entries.each_with_index do |assessment, index| %>
              <li>
                <span class="race-expectations-leader-rank" aria-hidden="true"><%= index + 1 %></span>
                <div class="race-expectations-leader-driver">
                  <%= link_to assessment.driver.fullname, driver_path(assessment.driver) %>
                  <small><%= assessment.row.constructor.name %> · Elo #<%= analysis_seed(assessment.seed) %> · Q<%= assessment.qualifying %></small>
                  <p>Expected <strong>P<%= number_with_precision(assessment.expected, precision: 1) %></strong> <span aria-hidden="true">→</span> Finished <strong>P<%= assessment.result.position_order %></strong></p>
                </div>
                <div class="race-expectations-leader-gap"><strong><%= analysis_signed(assessment.difference, precision: 1) %></strong><small>places</small></div>
              </li>
            <% end %>
          </ol>
        <% else %>
          <p class="race-expectations-leader-empty"><%= report.assessed_count.zero? ? "No comparable estimates available for this race yet." : "No classified finishers on this side of the estimate." %></p>
        <% end %>
      </article>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <p class="race-expectations-leaders-note"><strong><%= report.assessed_count %>/<%= report.assessments.size %> entrants assessed.</strong> Up to three per side, ranked by expected minus actual finish. DNFs, missing estimates and gaps rounding to 0.0 are excluded. “Flop” means below the model's estimate—not poor driving. A ranked gap can still be inside the usual error range.</p>
</section>
